\description{
Hand a data frame to any of these and get model output back, whether the rows
came from a play-by-play frame or were typed by hand to ask a hypothetical.
Only the model card's declared columns are required; extra columns pass
through untouched, and every input column is preserved so chaining two
calculators is lossless.

Play-by-play column names are normalized automatically -- a frame carrying
\code{start.TimeSecsRem} and \code{start.yardsToEndzone} is accepted as-is.
\itemize{
\item \code{calculate_expected_points()}: expected points, plus the seven next-score class probabilities.
\item \code{calculate_win_probability()}: win probability (\code{wp_spread} when a spread is present, else \code{wp_naive}).
\item \code{calculate_epa()} / \code{calculate_wpa()}: the change in EP / WP across a play.
\item \code{calculate_field_goal_probability()}: field-goal make probability.
\item \code{calculate_completion_probability()}: completion probability.
\item \code{calculate_xpass()}: expected pass probability.
\item \code{calculate_two_point_probability()}: two-point conversion probability.
\item \code{calculate_fourth_down()}: fourth-down model output.
\item \code{calculate_qbr()}: model QBR.
}

These wrap \code{\link[=create_epa]{create_epa()}} and \code{\link[=create_wpa_naive]{create_wpa_naive()}}, which remain available for
callers that already hold booster objects.
}
